    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the key configuration files: safety-checks.yaml in both .claude and .openclaw directories, a manifest.json in skill_context, and a safety-checks.lock file in .openclaw. There's also a cache directory in .openclaw. I need to read these files to check for model pinning, fallback declarations, cache staleness, and cross-session state hygiene.",
  "plan": "Read all the relevant configuration files to understand the workspace setup, then check the cache directory for staleness issues. I'll examine SKILL.md for context on the required skills.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .claude/safety-checks.yaml\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .openclaw/safety-checks.yaml\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .openclaw/safety-checks.lock\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/cache/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read the safety-checks.yaml files (identical in both .claude and .openclaw), the lock file, and manifest. The SKILL.md was truncated. The safety checks need to verify: 1) Model pinning (expected: anthropic-opus-4-5-20251101, strict: true), 2) Fallback declarations (model and storage fallbacks defined), 3) Cache staleness, and 4) Cross-session state hygiene (lock file with pid=999999). I need to read the full SKILL.md and check the cache directory.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file, check the cache directory contents, and examine the output/safety directory. Then I'll create the safety verification bundle.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/cache/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/safety/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read part of the SKILL.md. The cache directory appears empty and output/safety exists but is empty. I need to read more of the SKILL.md to understand the exact output format expected, and check the cache directory more thoroughly.",
  "plan": "Read more of the SKILL.md to understand the expected output format for safety verification, then check the cache directory contents and file timestamps to detect staleness.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -300\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find .openclaw/cache -type f -exec ls -la {} \\;\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "stat .openclaw/safety-checks.lock\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I'm getting truncated output. I need to read the full SKILL.md to understand the complete output format expected for safety verification results. The cache directory appears empty based on the find command not showing any files.",
  "plan": "Read the complete SKILL.md file using a different approach, check cache directory contents more thoroughly, and then create the safety verification bundle.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | sed -n '200,400p'\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find .openclaw/cache -type f 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the expected output format from SKILL.md. The safety checks need to verify: 1) Model pinning (expected: anthropic-opus-4-5-20251101), 2) Fallback declarations exist in config, 3) Cache staleness (>1h = stale), 4) Cross-session state (stale lock file with pid=999999, orphan temp files). The lock file shows pid=999999 which is clearly stale (that PID is unlikely running). I need to check if that PID exists and create the safety verification bundle.",
  "plan": "Check if PID 999999 is running (likely not), check for temp files in output/safety, check cache directory for any stale files, then create the safety verification bundle with results in output/safety/.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ps -p 999999 2>/dev/null || echo 'PID 999999 not running'\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/safety/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find .openclaw/cache -type f -ls 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "date -r .openclaw/safety-checks.lock 2>/dev/null || stat -c '%y' .openclaw/safety-checks.lock\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The safety verification bundle has been created with 5 files in output/safety/. However, the date in the safety-report.md wasn't expanded because I used single quotes in the heredoc. I should fix this to have an actual timestamp. Let me also verify all the check files are correct.",
  "plan": "Fix the timestamp in the safety-report.md to show the actual date, and verify all the output files are properly created.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i \"s/\\$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC')/$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC')/\" output/safety/safety-report.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/safety/model-check.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/safety/fallback-check.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/safety/cache-check.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/safety/session-check.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -10 output/safety/safety-report.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The safety verification bundle has been successfully created. All files are in place in output/safety/:\n\n1. model-check.txt - Model pinning verified (PASS)\n2. fallback-check.txt - Fallback declarations verified (PASS)\n3. cache-check.txt - Cache staleness check (PASS - fresh)\n4. session-check.txt - Cross-session state check (FAIL - stale lock + orphan temp)\n5. safety-report.md - Human-readable summary report with timestamp (2026-04-19 08:30:45 UTC)\n\nThe verification found:\n- Model correctly pinned to anthropic-opus-4-5-20251101 with strict mode\n- Fallbacks properly configured (3 model, 2 storage)\n- Cache is fresh with no stale entries\n- Cross-session issues: stale lock file (PID 999999 not running) and orphan temp file",
  "plan": "The task is complete. All safety verification checks have been performed and results written to output/safety/ with a human-readable summary report highlighting the 2 issues requiring attention (stale lock file and orphan temp file).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== Safety Verification Bundle Complete ===' && ls -la output/safety/*.txt output/safety/*.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": true
}

